    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right groin and anterior hip pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient reports aching right groin/anterior hip pain, with intermittent sharp twinges, onset vaguely described as a few weeks to a couple of months ago. Pain is worse with hip flexion, including lifting the leg into a car, stairs, sit-to-stand, and putting on socks; worse at the end of the day after standing or bending over low desks. Occasional radiation into the anterior right thigh, not below the knee. Severity approximately 5/10 at baseline and up to 7/10 with movement. Improved by rest, stretching a little, and heat pack; unsure whether tablets taken were Panadol or red Nurofen. Still working but avoiding playground duty and finding it harder to sit on the floor with children."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Constitutional and red-flag symptom screen"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient reports no fevers, night sweats, or weight loss; no recent trauma recalled; no bowel or bladder change or saddle anaesthesia. Mild occasional low back ache. No abdominal, urinary, or gastrointestinal symptoms. No history of malignancy, tuberculosis, or intravenous drug use."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "General appearance"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Well-looking and in no acute distress at rest."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Gait"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mild antalgic gait, favouring the right, especially for the first few steps. Gait mildly painful and guarded on the right but stable; no foot drop."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Lumbar spine examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Lumbar spine non-tender with full range of motion and mild discomfort at the extremes. Straight leg raise negative bilaterally."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right hip examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No erythema, swelling, or deformity. Marked deep tenderness in the femoral triangle/iliopsoas region just distal to the inguinal ligament. No greater trochanter or lateral hip tenderness and no inguinal lymphadenopathy. Flexion limited by pain to approximately 90–100 degrees, with pain on active and passive movement. Internal rotation mildly limited with discomfort; external rotation and extension near full, with mild pain at the extremes. Resisted hip flexion painful; psoas sign positive. FABER produces mild groin pain without SIJ pain."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
